WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:09.000
Sadly, about 85% of on-site makeup services currently operating are unlicensed.

2
00:00:09.336 --> 00:00:15.336
The surest way to check legitimacy is to see whether there's an actual physical shop address.

3
00:00:15.672 --> 00:00:21.120
Freelancers operating only through social media, with no address, leave it unclear who's responsible if something goes wrong.

4
00:00:21.456 --> 00:00:26.856
When booking, don't hesitate to ask, "Can you issue a cash receipt or take card payment?"

5
00:00:27.192 --> 00:00:30.456
A legitimate business should naturally be able to do that.

6
00:00:30.792 --> 00:00:34.224
That's only possible if they're registered as a business.

7
00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:43.176
Also, checking whether they hold a proper cosmetologist's license and business permit issued by the local district office is the wisest way to protect your precious day.

8
00:00:43.512 --> 00:00:47.208
A legitimate shop serves you with trust and accountability, but

9
00:00:47.544 --> 00:00:54.816
an unregistered, shopless freelancer often just stops answering the phone if something goes wrong.

10
00:00:55.152 --> 00:01:02.376
On your precious wedding day, be wise enough to choose a legitimate, professional service instead of an unlicensed one.
